      "status": "source checked",
      "correspondence": "Lagrange's theorem gives |M| · m = 0 on M and hence |M| · f = 0 on the Cartier dual M^* = Hom(M, (K^{sep})^×); with (|M| : K) ≠ 0, top-level local Galois finiteness and cohomological dimension two give finiteness of H^t(G_K, M) and H^t(G_K, M^*) for all t ≥ 0 and subsingleton H^t(G_K, M) for t ≥ 3. Over a finite extension K/ℚ_ℓ inside ℚ̄_ℓ, characteristic 0 makes |M| ≠ 0 in K unconditionally, and transporting along the discrete-module cohomology equivalences proves the ℤ/ℓ^rℤ local finiteness interface.",
      "review": "Checked strict disjointness from PTD-02 on GcohTop.lean ([13,15] vs [11,12]) and TensorHomDualRepRootsOfUnityIsoCartierPairing.lean ([111,129] vs [20,110] and [130,185]); verified characteristic-0 nonvanishing (|M| : K) ≠ 0 even when |M| is a power of ℓ, and Euler-characteristic check on ℚ_ℓ (odd ℓ and ℓ = 2)."
