    {
      "id": "PTD-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-poitou-tate-duality",
      "title": "Poitou–Tate global duality, Shafarevich–Tate pairing, nine-term exact sequence, and conjugation compatibility",
      "hypotheses": "A number field K (or F inside an algebraic closure Ω), a finite set S of finite places containing all primes dividing a positive integer N (or a prime power ℓ^r with r ≥ 1), the archimedean exclusion hypothesis that N is odd or K is totally complex (equivalently ℓ ≠ 2 or F is totally complex), chosen prolongations of the places in S, a finite discrete module M over the Galois group G_{K,S} unramified outside S killed by N (or over ℤ/ℓ^rℤ), a primitive ℓ^r-th root of unity ζ ∈ Ω for normalized local invariants, global Artin reciprocity CFT-01, local finiteness PTD-01, and local Tate duality PTD-02.",
      "statement": "(1) Compact-support global duality: for every r + s = 3, H^r_c(G_{K,S}, M) ≅ Hom(H^s(G_{K,S}, M'), ℚ/ℤ), where M' = Hom(M, μ_N). (2) Shafarevich–Tate duality: the locally trivial cohomology kernels Ш^1_S(K, M) and Ш^2_S(K, M') are finite and canonically Pontryagin dual via a bijective pairing in both directions. (3) Nine-term exact sequence: the global-to-local restriction maps in degrees 0, 1, 2, the local Tate duals of restriction in degrees 2, 1, 0 for M', and the connecting transgression maps fit into an exact nine-term sequence from 0 → H^0(G_{K,S}, M) through ∏_{v∈S} H^2(K_v, M) → H^0(G_{K,S}, M')^∨ → 0. (4) Normalized and conjugation-compatible interface: for every prime ℓ, r ≥ 1, (ℓ ≠ 2 or F totally complex), and primitive ℓ^r-th root ζ ∈ Ω, there exists a normalized family of bijective local invariants inv_A : H^2(D_A, μ_{ℓ^r}) ≃ ℤ/ℓ^rℤ satisfying the nine-term exact sequence, Shafarevich–Tate duality, and vanishing H^n(G_{F,S}, M) = 0 for all n ≥ 3; moreover, any normalized family of bijective local invariants is automatically conjugation-compatible under field automorphisms of Ω preserving F.",
      "definitions": [
        "Galois group G_{K,S} unramified outside S and locally trivial kernel Ш^i_S(K, M) = ker(H^i(G_{K,S}, M) → ∏_{v∈S} H^i(K_v, M))",
        "compact-support global cohomology H^r_c(G_{K,S}, M) and nine-term Poitou–Tate exact sequence",
        "ζ-normalized local invariants inv_A (sending Kummer-unramified cup cocycles of local uniformizers to 1) and conjugation compatibility under automorphisms of Ω"
